import{_ as t,o as a,c as i,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const m=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Entry 815 | Transcended Ones and Laws | The Transcended One's Practice of the Law-First Axiom","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 815 | Transcended Ones and Laws | The Transcended One's Practice of the Law-First Axiom","no":815,"module":4,"tags":["Transcended One","Laws","Law-First Axiom","Setting Self-Consistency","Book-Eating/Stale-Ending"],"related":["09-Reality-as-Base Fundamental Stance","03-Symbiotic-Civilization Charter","709-Unity of Transcendence and the Law-First Axiom"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0815_模块4-超脱者与法则-法则优先公理超脱者实践.md","filePath":"en/0815_模块4-超脱者与法则-法则优先公理超脱者实践.md"}`),o={name:"en/0815_模块4-超脱者与法则-法则优先公理超脱者实践.md"};function s(r,e,l,c,h,d){return a(),i("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="entry-815-transcended-ones-and-laws-the-transcended-one-s-practice-of-the-law-first-axiom" tabindex="-1">Entry 815 | Transcended Ones and Laws | The Transcended One&#39;s Practice of the Law-First Axiom <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-815-transcended-ones-and-laws-the-transcended-one-s-practice-of-the-law-first-axiom" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 815 | Transcended Ones and Laws | The Transcended One&#39;s Practice of the Law-First Axiom&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 4 · Transcendence Orthodox Definition Library | Benchmark base: Documents 09, 03, 709</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-the-law-first-axiom-is-not-a-slogan-but-a-multiple-choice-the-transcended-one-must-make-every-day" tabindex="-1">Introduction: the law-first axiom is not a slogan, but a multiple-choice the transcended one must make every day <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-the-law-first-axiom-is-not-a-slogan-but-a-multiple-choice-the-transcended-one-must-make-every-day" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: the law-first axiom is not a slogan, but a multiple-choice the transcended one must make every day&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The law-first axiom is the most special of the six top-level axioms — unlike the other four that directly prescribe &quot;what to do,&quot; it prescribes &quot;the priority among all prescriptions&quot;: <strong>laws first, never eat books, never go stale; setting self-consistency above plot convenience; plot may not hijack setting.</strong> This axiom sounds abstract, but in the transcended one&#39;s daily work, it is a multiple-choice faced at every decision moment. The sixth, the universal equal infinite law, establishes the origin logic that all beings inherently possess basic infinite power and predation loses its meaning.</p><p>The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><p>Six top-level axioms in this entry centrally discuss the law-first axiom itself: why does it stand above the other four? Because if the setting is not self-consistent, the other four axioms cannot stably run — energy conservation broken, the anti-predation axiom loses its physical base; laws may be casually changed by plot, and the republican guarantee becomes empty talk. So the law-first axiom is the meta-axiom; it guards the other axioms&#39; stability.</p><p>This article focuses: in daily work, how the transcended one turns the law-first axiom from &quot;text written in the charter&quot; into &quot;practice executed at every decision.&quot;</p><h2 id="i-the-law-first-axiom-s-three-layer-meaning" tabindex="-1">I. The Law-First Axiom&#39;s Three-Layer Meaning <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-the-law-first-axiom-s-three-layer-meaning" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. The Law-First Axiom&#39;s Three-Layer Meaning&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The law-first axiom has three progressive layers of meaning:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Layer</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Concrete Requirement</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Layer 1: laws above plot</td><td>The development of any civilizational event may not violate established law setting</td><td>If plot needs conflict with laws, change the plot, not the laws</td></tr><tr><td>Layer 2: self-consistency above convenience</td><td>Temporarily modifying setting for plot convenience is the highest-level violation</td><td>Temporarily changing setting = book-eating; once it occurs, must be publicly corrected</td></tr><tr><td>Layer 3: expansion without collapse</td><td>The worldview may infinitely expand, but the expanded part must be self-consistent with existing setting</td><td>When new content conflicts with old setting, old setting prevails, adjust new content</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Three layers together: <strong>laws are hard constraints; plot is soft variables.</strong> All the transcended one&#39;s work proceeds within the law framework — he may not, because &quot;a hero moment is needed,&quot; let some cultivator violate energy conservation and suddenly grow stronger; may not, because &quot;a moving moment is needed,&quot; let some already-dead cultivator violate causality and resurrect. Laws are the ceiling; plot may not break through the ceiling.</p><h2 id="ii-three-typical-plot-hijack-scenarios-the-transcended-one-faces" tabindex="-1">II. Three Typical &quot;Plot-Hijack&quot; Scenarios the Transcended One Faces <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-three-typical-plot-hijack-scenarios-the-transcended-one-faces" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Three Typical &quot;Plot-Hijack&quot; Scenarios the Transcended One Faces&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The law-first axiom in practice mainly guards against three typical &quot;plot-hijacks-setting&quot; scenarios:</p><ol><li><strong>Scenario 1: law conflict in emergency rescue.</strong> In a plane crisis, the transcended one faces a choice — follow legal procedure (may be too late to rescue), or bypass laws and directly rescue (violate procedure). The law-first axiom requires: bypassing laws to directly rescue is a violation. The correct approach is finding the fastest path within the law framework — emergency channels, plan activation, linked dispatch; these are fast-response mechanisms within the law framework, not &quot;temporarily breaking laws.&quot;</li><li><strong>Scenario 2: setting conflict in major breakthrough.</strong> Some cultivator&#39;s breakthrough direction is inconsistent with the established law definition — for example, he claims he &quot;broke energy conservation.&quot; The law-first axiom requires: this kind of &quot;breakthrough&quot; is not recognized. The cultivator must either adjust his own understanding, or propose modification suggestions through legal law-revision procedure (entry 814), rather than personally announcing &quot;I broke through the laws.&quot;</li><li><strong>Scenario 3: causal conflict in historical events.</strong> Cross-plane exploration discovers some historical event contradicts existing historical records. The law-first axiom requires: do not rush to &quot;rewrite history&quot; to accommodate new discoveries, but first verify the new discovery&#39;s authenticity — if the new discovery is indeed reliable, systematically correct historical records through civilizational-correction procedure (entry 828), not casually change a detail.</li></ol><p>Three scenarios&#39; common solution: <strong>when encountering conflict, do not move laws; move the plan.</strong> Laws are constants; the plan is the variable — always adjust the plan to fit laws, never adjust laws to fit the plan.</p><h2 id="iii-the-transcended-one-s-book-eating-self-review-mechanism" tabindex="-1">III. The Transcended One&#39;s &quot;Book-Eating&quot; Self-Review Mechanism <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-the-transcended-one-s-book-eating-self-review-mechanism" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. The Transcended One&#39;s &quot;Book-Eating&quot; Self-Review Mechanism&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Before executing any law-level operation, the transcended one must perform a &quot;book-eating risk&quot; self-review. Review checklist:</p><ul><li>Does this operation contradict an established fundamental law? If yes, stop the operation.</li><li>Does this operation require temporarily modifying some operating law? If yes, transfer to the law-revision democratic procedure (entry 814); do not do a temporary modification.</li><li>Will this operation&#39;s consequences contradict existing historical records? If yes, first verify, then correct; do not casually change history.</li><li>Will this operation give some cultivator &quot;abilities laws do not allow&quot;? If yes, refuse to grant.</li></ul><p>Four review questions; any one answered &quot;yes,&quot; the operation immediately pauses. This is not cowardice, but the law-first axiom&#39;s daily discipline — <strong>better slower than book-eating.</strong> Eat a book once, the law network&#39;s credibility drops one point; eat ten, the whole civilization&#39;s setting foundation shakes.</p><h2 id="iv-why-the-transcended-one-must-take-the-lead-in-obeying-the-law-first-axiom" tabindex="-1">IV. Why the Transcended One Must Take the Lead in Obeying the Law-First Axiom <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-why-the-transcended-one-must-take-the-lead-in-obeying-the-law-first-axiom" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Why the Transcended One Must Take the Lead in Obeying the Law-First Axiom&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The transcended one is law-anchor authority&#39;s holder — he theoretically has the ability to &quot;operate laws.&quot; Precisely because of this, he even more may not become &quot;the first person to break laws.&quot; Three reasons:</p><ul><li><strong>Demonstration effect</strong>: the transcended one is Myriad Ranks&#39; example. If he himself does not obey the law-first axiom, Myriad-Rank cultivators will feel &quot;laws are for ordinary people; strong ones are exceptions&quot; — this is the breeding ground for predation-ism&#39;s revival.</li><li><strong>Trust base</strong>: Myriad Ranks gave law-anchor authority to the transcended one; the trust base is that he will not abuse this authority. If he modifies laws for convenience, Myriad Ranks&#39; trust in him instantly collapses — his civilizational weight directly zeroes.</li><li><strong>System stability</strong>: the law network is a self-consistent system. The transcended one&#39;s one private law modification may trigger chain reactions he did not anticipate. Book-eating&#39;s cost is not just &quot;setting inconsistency,&quot; but the whole law network&#39;s systematic risk.</li></ul><p>So, the transcended one obeying the law-first axiom is not because &quot;he doesn&#39;t dare,&quot; but because <strong>he is the person who most clearly understands the cost of violating laws.</strong></p><h2 id="v-five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">V. Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><p><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: book-eating self-review avoids repeated engineering waste of &quot;after revising find it wrong and change back,&quot; and also avoids systematic repair costs caused by law conflicts</p></li><li><p><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: the law-first axiom seals the channel of &quot;strong ones under plot-need name bypassing laws to predate&quot; — you may not rob by saying &quot;plot needs it&quot;</p></li><li><p><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo authors change setting for thrill points at any time; book-eating/stale-ending is the norm; Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s transcended one takes &quot;not eating books&quot; as daily discipline, every operation passing book-eating-risk review</p></li><li><p><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: the law-first axiom applies equally to all Myriad-Rank cultivators — transcended ones are no exception, ordinary cultivators are no exception; before laws there is no privileged class</p></li><li><p><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: the law-first axiom&#39;s three-layer meaning, three typical scenarios, and self-review checklist are all publicly queryable; Myriad Ranks may supervise whether the transcended one strictly obeys</p></li><li><p>Terminology alignment: the Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm is this batch&#39;s standard realm appellation; Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision monitors operation compliance throughout; the Myriad-Origin two-way cycle ensures energy and knowledge circulate perpetually among Myriad Ranks.</p></li><li><p><strong>Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law</strong>: all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity — infinite origin inherent in all; predation naturally loses its meaning</p></li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The transcended one&#39;s practice of the law-first axiom turns &quot;setting self-consistency above plot convenience&quot; from a manifesto into discipline at every decision moment. In daily work the transcended one faces countless temptations of &quot;should we bypass laws for convenience,&quot; and every time he chooses &quot;not bypass,&quot; he adds a brick to civilization&#39;s setting foundation. He is not incapable of bypassing laws — he is law-anchor authority&#39;s holder, he has that ability — but he chooses not to bypass, because he most clearly knows: <strong>laws bypassed once, civilization shrinks one inch.</strong> When the transcended one takes the lead in guarding the law-first axiom, Myriad Ranks&#39; civilizational mansion may forever not collapse amid infinite expansion.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/09-现实为基根本立场.html">Entry 09 · Reality-as-Base Fundamental Stance</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/03-共生文明宪章.html">Entry 03 · Symbiotic-Civilization Charter</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/709_模块4-超脱与法则优先公理的统一.html">Entry 709 · Unity of Transcendence and the Law-First Axiom</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/811_模块4-超脱者与法则-总论.html">Entry 811 · Transcended Ones and Laws Overview</a></li></ul>',29)])])}const p=t(o,[["render",s]]);export{m as __pageData,p as default};
